  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the dehumanizing comparison scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the overall juxtaposed_comparison_scene, which functions as a dehumanizing visual and textual construct. The meme's structure, particularly the bottom text 'i can't tell the difference', implicitly invites the user to adopt the perspective of the stereotype — to see Michelle Obama as visually indistinguishable from a primate. This projection is not explicit with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but it is implicit in the meme's rhetorical framing, which forces the viewer to confront the racist trope and potentially internalize or endorse the dehumanizing comparison. The user is thus projected onto the scene as the one who must 'see' the equivalence, making them complicit in the projection of the anti-Black primate stereotype.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
